# Hovertemplate

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:plotly_ex, "~> 0.3"},
  {:kino, "~> 0.18"}
])
```

## Section

`hovertemplate` gives full control over the hover label content. Use `%{x}`,
`%{y}`, `%{text}`, and D3 format strings like `%{y:.2f}`. End with
`<extra></extra>` to suppress the default secondary box showing the trace name.

```elixir
alias Plotly.{Figure, Scatter}

Figure.new()
|> Figure.add_trace(
  Scatter.new(
    x: ["Jan", "Feb", "Mar", "Apr"],
    y: [1200, 950, 1400, 1100],
    mode: "lines+markers",
    hovertemplate: "Month: %{x}<br>Revenue: $%{y:,.0f}<extra></extra>",
    name: "Revenue"
  )
)
|> Figure.update_layout(title: "Custom Hovertemplate")
|> Plotly.show()
```

Use `%{text}` to reference an extra text array:

```elixir
Figure.new()
|> Figure.add_trace(
  Scatter.new(
    x: [1, 2, 3],
    y: [4, 5, 6],
    mode: "markers",
    text: ["Point A", "Point B", "Point C"],
    hovertemplate: "%{text}<br>(%{x}, %{y})<extra></extra>",
    marker: %{size: 12}
  )
)
|> Figure.update_layout(title: "Hovertemplate with Extra Text")
|> Plotly.show()
```
